Description: Methods for estimating average treatment effects (ATE) and
    conditional average treatment effects (CATE) in randomized trials and
    observational studies with binary, count or time-to-event outcomes.
    The package provides doubly robust ATE estimation and CATE score fitting,
    with tools for cross-validation and visualization of CATE prediction models.
    For time-to-event outcomes,
    the package estimates restricted mean survival and marginal cumulative
    hazard ratios at a specified horizon, using outcome and censoring models.
    Ratio-based methods for treatment-covariate interactions build on
    Yadlowsky et al. (2020) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2020.1772080>.
    The visualization and interpretation of individualized treatment rules are
    discussed by Jiang et al. (2026) <doi:10.1201/9781003300809-20>.
